cting 200) so the fix is confirmed at the edge, not only in the rendered template text.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5375,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC#2: 'live fetchability is only observable after a deploy, which is out of scope for this ticket'","The bug itself is 'rendered/deployed config did not route the path' — a template-only assertion does not close the loop the ticket opened","E5 note: structural greps ARE legitimate, so this is a coaching gap not a change-detector MAJOR"],"finding":"The entire fix (edge routing correctness) is validated ONLY by a unit test that renders the template and greps for the location-block text; there is no live/end-to-end verification that GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp actually returns 200 at the edge after deploy. The rendered config can contain a syntactically-correct block yet still not resolve live (e.g. proxy_pass URI semantics differ from intent, the mcp-upstream include is empty at deploy time, or location-match ordering behaves unexpectedly under real nginx) — which is precisely the failure class this ticket exists to fix (config looked fine, live returned 404).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7ed88465b90ed13b","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing / Acceptance Criteria (AC#2)","norm_id":"nffa9ab61628d7d8b","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add an acceptance line: after deploy, `curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp` returns 200; note it as a manual/ops verification if it cannot run in-session.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Ground the claim that the app returns 200 for the `/mcp`-suffixed PRM path (`/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp`) with in-repo evidence — the only existing test (test_mcp_auth.py:366) exercises the UN-suffixed `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource`; confirm the exact path the MCP SDK serves and reconcile the no-path `proxy_pass` choice with it (contrast the working exact-match blocks that use `proxy_pass http://rebar_mcp/mcp`).","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.42,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan asserts: 'the app direct on 127.0.0.1:8091 returns 200 for /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp' — cited to an out-of-repo box probe and 'the RCA comment', neither in the material under review.","Repo counter-evidence: tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_auth.py:366 fetches `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` (NO `/mcp` suffix) and asserts 200 — the only in-repo demonstration of what the app serves.","The PRM route is delegated to the MCP SDK: search_files for 'oauth-protected-resource' and 'resource_metadata' under src/ returns no repo route definition, so the served path is an SDK behavior not settleable by repo grep; resolve_symbol on the SDK route returned UNRESOLVED.","The plan's chosen `proxy_pass http://rebar_mcp;` (no URI path, verbatim URI) differs from the existing WORKING exact-match blocks which rewrite the URI via `proxy_pass http://rebar_mcp/mcp` (rebar.conf.template:158,179) — making the served-path assumption decisive to correctness."],"finding":"The load-bearing premise 'the app on 127.0.0.1:8091 returns 200 for /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp' (the /mcp-suffixed PRM path) is unverifiable from the repo and is contradicted by the only in-repo evidence, which exercises the UN-suffixed path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd2d2ce7ab99c1320","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause section ('probed from the box, the app direct on 127.0.0.1:8091 returns 200 for /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp') and Approach ('proxy_pass http://rebar_mcp; with NO URI path ... the app already answers with 200').","norm_id":"nb31c67e1055e05fd","priority":0.33,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the SDK serves the PRM only at the un-suffixed `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource`, the new verbatim-URI location forwards `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp` to the app, which 404s — the edge fix ships but the advertised URL still returns 404."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"State the rollback path explicitly: reverting the single `location =` block in the template and redeploying restores prior behavior with no data cleanup.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T12"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Change touches infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template deployed via the referenced blue-green flip","No explicit 'to undo: revert this location block and redeploy' statement in the plan","The change is additive exact-match so revert is cheap and data-free — hence a light coaching note, not a MAJOR"],"finding":"The plan changes the runtime routing behavior of the deployed nginx edge but does not state an explicit rollback step. The change is trivially reversible (revert the single template line, redeploy), but the plan should say so given it is an edge-config change to a live server.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f52151eed54ef0ffb","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope","norm_id":"n994c487a09332da9","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5714,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Tie the 'app returns 200 at the suffixed path' claim to its mechanism — the MCP SDK's RFC 9728 path-insertion driven by auth_resource_server_url=.../mcp/ — rather than the live probe alone, so the app-half claim is verifiable from the spec.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the app direct on 127.0.0.1:8091 returns 200 for /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp while the edge returns 404'","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_auth.py:366 exercises client.get('/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource') — the UN-suffixed path — so the repo does not itself evidence the suffixed 200","RFC 9728 (rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9728.html, retrieved): a resource identifier with a path component has /.well-known/ + suffix inserted between host and path, terminating slash removed — so auth_resource_server_url .../mcp/ (docs/mcp-auth.md:252) yields exactly the suffixed advertised path"],"finding":"The load-bearing capability assertion — 'the app direct on 127.0.0.1:8091 returns 200 for /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp' — is grounded only on a live box probe; the sole in-repo PRM test serves the UN-suffixed /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource, and the suffixed form is produced by the MCP SDK's RFC 9728 path-insertion (resource identifier .../mcp/ → suffix inserted between host and path). Naming that mechanism makes the assertion verifiable beyond the probe.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f19d870b56bae3d4f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause (confirmed, see the RCA comment)","norm_id":"na7099a204495e0a9","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the SDK/app version on the box changes how it derives the served PRM path, the edge route could once again point at a path the app does not answer, and the probe (not a repeatable check) would be the only thing that caught it"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In the Root cause section, add one sentence: the SDK serves the PRM at the well-known path derived from auth_resource_server_url's path component per RFC 9728 (host + /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource + /mcp), which is why the app answers 200 at the suffixed path the 401 advertises.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"23ae5da683d31149","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["6cc1d8175b82a594",5427],"description_boxes":["1a0f564ddc603945",0],"file_impact":["2dca00b8a90db9a3",2],